From fd17ad5394be7f66231329de53cf6eb085b8a7cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:22:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inventory): translate Bedrock cartography in core

Open cartography through ordinary Java menus and select creation, rename, clone, extension, lock, and locator operations from advertised recipes and retained map state. Preserve native slot identities, input consumption, naming filters, locked-copy requests, inventory acknowledgments, and crafted metadata synchronization across direct and proxy connections.

Native Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372 protocol 2193 captures establish recipe UUIDs, single lower-slot operations, locator subtype, sparse map families, and clone request counts. Single Shift-click crafts one pair; right-click does not split the two-map clone. Keep those behaviors instead of automatically repeating Java quick moves.

Ordinary Java uses a nonce-bound text dialog for naming because its cartography screen has no name field. Native inline naming and operation previews still need client rendering work and integration verification. Seven focused tests cover recipe selection, item identity, metadata preservation, request construction, and complete-result placement.

Advertise versioned cartography presentation state before opening the menu.
Include edit acknowledgements so client rendering can retain newer typing
while older name echoes arrive through ViaProxy. Export native UI images
from the effective pack stack and invalidate converted pack caches.
